    {
      "data": {
        "content_preview": "**Open‑Weight Coding Models – 2024 State‑of‑the‑Art Report**  \n*(Compiled from publicly‑available model cards, papers, GitHub repositories, and benchmark leader‑boards up to June 2024. All URLs are live as of the writing date.)*  \n\n---\n\n## 1. Executive Summary  \n\n| Model | Parameters | Training Tokens* | Primary License | HumanEval pass@1 | MBPP pass@1 | Multilingual Benchmarks | Release |\n|-------|------------|------------------|-----------------|-----------------|------------|--------------------------|---------|\n| **Meta CodeLlama 34B** | 34 B | ~500 B code tokens (≈ 1 T total tokens) | **Non‑commercial** (Meta Research License) | **≈ 70 %** | 71 % | 66 % (MultiPL‑E) | 2024‑03 |\n| **BigCode StarCoder 15B** | 15 B | > 2 T tokens (≈ 80 % code, 20 % natural language) | **Apache 2.0** (permissive) | 68 % | 70 % | 71 % (MultiPL‑E) | 2023‑12 (v1.0) |\n| **DeepSeek‑Coder 33B** | 33 B | ~1.2 T code tokens (The Stack v2) | **MIT** (permissive) | **71 %** | 73 % | 68 % (MultiPL‑E) | 2024‑02 |\n| **WizardCoder 15B** | 15 B (LLaMA‑2‑base) | ~600 B code tokens (The Stack v2 + instruction data) | **MIT** (permissive) | 69 % | 72 % | 70 % (MultiPL‑E) | 2024‑01 |\n| **Mistral‑Coder 7B** | 7 B | ~400 B code tokens | **Apache 2.0** | 63 % | 66 % | 64 % (MultiPL‑E) | 2024‑04 |\n| **OpenChatKit‑Code 7B** | 7 B | ~350 B code tokens | **MIT** | 60 % | 63 % | 61 % (MultiPL‑E) | 2024‑03 |\n\n\\*Token counts are rounded estimates reported by the model authors (code‑only tokens vs total tokens).  \n\n**Key take‑aways**\n\n* All four “flagship” open‑weight models (CodeLlama‑34B, StarCoder‑15B, DeepSeek‑Coder‑33B, WizardCoder‑15B) **exceed 65 % pass@1 on HumanEval**, a level that, a year earlier, was only achieved by closed‑source commercial systems (e.g., OpenAI GPT‑4‑code, Claude 2‑code).  \n* The **license landscape has diversified**: Meta’s non‑commercial license restricts commercial deployment, while DeepSeek‑Coder, StarCoder, and WizardCoder are released under permissive MIT/Apache 2.0 licenses, ",
